== pitboard
Switch Claude Code, Codex and Claude Desktop between your own accounts without signing out, and see
what each Claude Code and Codex account has left

Usage: pitboard [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status       What is signed in, and how much each Claude Code and Codex account has left (the
               default)
  use          Switch a tool to an enrolled account
  enroll       Add an account: the one signed in now, or with --sign-in, another one
  rename       Change the label an account is enrolled under
  forget       Drop an account and its parked login
  watch        Switch Claude Code before the account in use runs out, and warm up accounts
  warm         Start an account's five-hour period early, so it resets sooner
  statusline   One line for Claude Code's status bar; reads its session JSON on stdin
  renew        Renew every parked login that is due, and nothing else
  schedule     Keep parked logins alive without running anything yourself
  vault        Where parked logins are kept: in the login keychain
  log          What Pitboard has changed, and when
  doctor       Check that what Pitboard relies on still holds on this machine
  uninstall    Delete every parked login this Pitboard wrote, the daily renewal schedule, the watch
               service and Pitboard's own files
  stow         Put away the login Claude Code left in a file behind the keychain, then delete the
               file
  repair       Ask the credential store what parked logins are here, and account for every one
  abandon      Give up on an interrupted switch that cannot be finished, keeping every login
  adopt        Take over a Pitboard directory another computer wrote, keeping the accounts
  completions  Print a shell completion script
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

Examples:
  pitboard enroll personal        Add the account Claude Code is signed in to
  pitboard enroll work --sign-in  Sign in to another account and add it
  pitboard use work               Switch Claude Code to work

== pitboard status
What is signed in, and how much each Claude Code and Codex account has left (the default)

Usage: pitboard status [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

      --offline
          Answer from what was last measured, without asking anyone

      --fresh
          Ask about every account, even one asked about moments ago

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard use
Switch a tool to an enrolled account

Usage: pitboard use [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under, such as `work`, `codex/work` or `desktop/work`

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -y, --yes
          Where the service refuses the login in use for good, put this account's login in its place
          without asking; needed without a terminal or with `--json`

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard enroll
Add an account: the one signed in now, or with --sign-in, another one

Usage: pitboard enroll [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          A short name for this account, such as `personal` or `work`. `codex/work` names a Codex
          account, `desktop/work` a Claude Desktop one; a bare name means Claude Code

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

      --sign-in
          Sign in to another account first, through the tool's own sign-in

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard rename
Change the label an account is enrolled under

Usage: pitboard rename [OPTIONS] <FROM> <TO>

Arguments:
  <FROM>
          The label it has now

  <TO>
          The label it should have

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard forget
Drop an account and its parked login

Usage: pitboard forget [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label to drop

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -y, --yes
          Do not ask first; needed without a terminal or with `--json`

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard watch
Switch Claude Code before the account in use runs out, and warm up accounts

Usage: pitboard watch [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  install    Have this computer's own service manager run `pitboard watch` from now on and at each
             sign-in
  status     Say whether it is installed
  uninstall  Stop it and take it away
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --at <PERCENT>
          Switch once a limit of the account in use reaches this share, from 50 to 99
          
          [default: 95]

      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

      --once
          Decide once whether to switch, from the usage Pitboard last measured, asking no service
          for usage, and stop. Warms nothing up

  -h, --help
          Print help

Anthropic's terms may cover automatic switching and warm-ups:
https://docs.usepitboard.com/concepts/limits#is-this-allowed

