== pitboard warm
Start an account's five-hour period early, so it resets sooner

Usage: pitboard warm [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  now    Start an account's five-hour period now, whatever the span, through one short request
         Claude Code makes with that account's login
  on     Warm up an account from now on, within the span `range` sets
  off    Stop warming up an account
  range  Warm up accounts only between these times of each day, in this computer's time zone
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm now
Start an account's five-hour period now, whatever the span, through one short request Claude Code
makes with that account's login

Usage: pitboard warm now [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under, such as `work`

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm on
Warm up an account from now on, within the span `range` sets

Usage: pitboard warm on [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under, such as `work`

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm off
Stop warming up an account

Usage: pitboard warm off [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm range
Warm up accounts only between these times of each day, in this computer's time zone

Usage: pitboard warm range [OPTIONS] <FROM> <TO>

Arguments:
  <FROM>
          When to start, such as 06:00

  <TO>
          When to stop, such as 22:00; 00:00 and 24:00 are midnight, and a time before FROM runs
          past it

Options:
      --json
          Print JSON instead of text

  -h, --help
          Print help

